@0    = ~You're going to get hurt. That's all I'm saying. You throw yourself around the way you're doing, people will take advantage.~
@1    = ~Thou speakst not of what thou knowest. I love <CHARNAME> with all my heart.~
@2    = ~Look, I know what it's like. When I was your age I loved Olive Langford with all my heart - well, something like that, anyway - and it feels really intense, but it's not something to take so damn seriously!~
@3    = ~How darest thou question my regard! Thou and I have nothing in common. Nothing!~
@4    = ~You really are something. Sometimes when we fight, I--~
@5    = ~I cannot stand by and watch this.~
@6    = ~Okay, well, I'm just having a chat with <CHARNAME>, so if you want to shove off and leave us to it, I'd be happy.~
@7    = ~I shall not. <CHARNAME> is my love, and I am his.~
@8    = ~Uh-huh. <CHARNAME>, what the hell? With you leading her on like this, I'm not so sure you're worth my time anyway, but I'll give you the benefit of the doubt. Sure, she's attractive, but she's not exactly--~
@9    = ~Thou common rogue! I shall not listen to these...lewd suggestions toward <CHARNAME>! They are - are...~
@10   = ~<CHARNAME>, I beg of thee - please tell this scoundrel that there are no...impure intentions in your heart.~
@11   = ~It's true, Faren. I want to be with Saerileth always.~
@12   = ~Saerileth, I'm sorry. This thing with you is moving too quickly.~
@13   = ~O, thou wonder! Thou art a jewel amongst men, and I swear I shall love you forever!~
@14   = ~...~
@15   = ~Okay. You do that. <CHARNAME>, you're really not the guy I thought you were. I won't be bothering you in the future, believe me.~
@16   = ~But...but with this man? This impure--~
@17   = ~Hey, enough of that, if you please. <CHARNAME>, how's about we carry on that chat later?~
@18   = ~Just wondering, and don't bite my head off, but did you go to school over in Mount Celestia?~
@19   = ~I learnt all I needed from the priests of Tyr.~
@20   = ~And you're an only child, yeah?~
@21   = ~It is true. Whyfore askst thou?~
@22   = ~Was just... Saerileth, did you have any friends when you were little?~
@23   = ~Friends?~
@24   = ~Seems lonely, getting Chosen when you were so young. Really lonely.~
@25   = ~I see the pity in thine eyes, but there is no need for it. In Tyr's glory I have all the company I might desire.~
@26   = ~That's kind of what I was expecting.~
@27   = ~Okay, Saerileth, I'm going to buy you a present. The girls I used to know liked nice-smelling stuff to put in the bath, with these glittery bits in.~
@28   = ~I know it's not a surprise now, but I didn't want to end up getting the wrong thing.~
@29   = ~Faren, I do not desire a gift from thee. Thou needst not trouble yourself over such things.~
@30   = ~No trouble. I want to do it. Do you like rose or lavender?~
@31   = ~Well, I...had not...~
@32   = ~Mint?~
@33   = ~If thy heart is set upon this, I do cherish the scent of the lily.~
@34   = ~Excellent! One lily bath-thing, coming right up.~
@35   = ~Bath-thing? Faren, thou hast no idea what thou sayest!~
@36   = ~Hey, I live to serve. I'll sort it out, don't you worry!~
@37   = ~...but we rescued the actor in the end. He was pretty grateful - and so he should have been, with all the trouble we went to!~
@38   = ~It was thy duty to help this man. Tyr looks kindly upon those who do such.~
@39   = ~Yeah, we managed to get a nice lot of payment from the actor, too. Never knew those guys had so much nice jewellery.~
@40   = ~Thou wouldst extract payment for such a service? Virtue is its own reward, Faren!~
@41   = ~Hey, we had to eat. It would've been dumb not to squeeze him a little.~
@42   = ~I will not listen to this further! Thou art a scoundrel!~
